  "foaf:name": "All-Atlantic Floating University Network",
  "sdo:name": "All-Atlantic Floating University Network",
  "sdo:description": "The All-Atlantic Floating University Network, officially launched in December 2022, was created in the scope of the Joint Pilot Action developed under the EU-Funded Project AANChOR and in the framework of the All-Atlantic Ocean Research and Innovation Alliance (AAORIA). It is a collaborative network that connects 42 ongoing training-at-sea and/or floating university programs across 27 Atlantic countries. The network aims to maximise synergies among these initiatives, share best practices, and jointly develop strategies to expand training-at-sea opportunities for students and early-career ocean professionals throughout the Atlantic region.",
  "sdo:location": "Portugal",
  "sdo:identifier": "577",
  "sdo:url": "https://oceandecade.org/actions/all-atlantic-floating-university-network/",
  "sdo:license": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/",
